# Class: obo:FOODON_00002852 (Granny Smith apple tree)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_00002852 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00002852 "The Granny Smith is a tip-bearing apple cultivar, which originated in Australia in 1868. The tree is thought to be a hybrid of Malus sylvestris, the European wild apple, with the North American apple Malus pumila as the polleniser."@en)
