# Class: obo:FOODON_00002899 (goby)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00002899 "Goby is a common name for many species of small to medium sized ray-finned fish, normally with large heads and tapered bodies, which are found in marine, brackish and freshwater environments. Traditionally most of the species called gobies have been classified in the order Perciformes as the suborder Gobioidei but in the 5th Edition of Fishes of the World this suborder is elevated to an order Gobiiformes within the clade Percomorpha.[1] Not all the species in the Gobiiformes are referred to as gobies and the \"true gobies\" are placed in the family Gobiidae, while other species referred to as gobies have been placed in the Oxudercidae."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:FOODON_00002899 <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-8844-9165>)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:FOODON_00002899 "Emma Griffiths"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_00002899 wikipedia:Goby)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:date obo:FOODON_00002899 "2019-08-09T15:06:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_00002899 "goby"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_00002899 obo:FOODON_03411581)

# Class: obo:FOODON_00002900 (scad)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00002900 "A Scad fish is any of several species of fishes in the family Carangidae (order Perciformes), which also includes the jacks, amberjacks, and pompanos. The name scad is usually restricted to certain species in the genera Decapterus, Selar, and Trachurus. The half dozen species are marine and occur along the Atlantic coast of the Americas, except for the Mexican scad (D. scombrinus), which is found in the Pacific Ocean.[Encyclopedia Britannica, December 05, 2017; accessed August 09, 2019]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:FOODON_00002900 <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-8844-9165>)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:FOODON_00002900 "Emma Griffiths"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_00002900 <https://www.britannica.com/animal/scad>)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:date obo:FOODON_00002900 "2019-08-09T16:12:10Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_00002900 "scad"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_00002900 obo:FOODON_03411755)

# Class: obo:FOODON_00002901 (golden pompano)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00002901 "Golden pompanos are fairly deep bodied ocean fish of family Carangidae, and are prized eating fish worldwide. They can be distinguished from other pompanos by their slightly longer dorsal fin."@en)
