# Class: obo:FOODON_00002996 (mrigal carp)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_00002996 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00002996 "The mrigal carp (Cirrhinus cirrhosus), also known as the white carp, is a species of ray-finned fish in the carp family. Native to streams and rivers in India, the only surviving wild population is in the Cauvery River, leading to its IUCN rating as vulnerable."@en)
