# Class: obo:FOODON_03411064 (huckleberry plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411064 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411064 "Huckleberry is a name used in North America for several plants in two closely related genera in the family *Ericaceae: Gaylussacia* and *Vaccinium*. While some *Vaccinium* species, such as the Red Huckleberry, are always called huckleberries, other species may be called blueberries or huckleberries depending upon local custom. Similar Vaccinium species in Europe are called bilberries. Berries range in color according to species from bright red, through dark purple, and into the blues. In taste the berries range from tart to sweet, with a flavor similar to that of a blueberry, especially in blue/purple colored varieties. [Wikipedia : ]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411064 "WIKIPEDIA:Huckleberries")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411064 langual:B1064)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411064 "gaylussacia spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411064 "vaccinium spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411064 "huckleberry plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411064 obo:FOODON_03411614)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411067 (lime (citrus) plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411067 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411067 "A lime  is a hybrid citrus fruit, which is typically round, lime green, 3-6 centimetres (1.2-2.4 in) in diameter, and contains acidic juice vesicles. There are several species of citrus trees whose fruits are called limes, including the Key lime (*Citrus aurantifolia*), Persian lime, kaffir lime, and desert lime. Limes are a rich source of vitamin C, sour and are often used to accent the flavours of foods and beverages. They are grown year-round. Plants with fruit called \"limes\" have diverse genetic origins; limes do not form a monophyletic group. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(fruit)]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411067 <http://eol.org/pages/4414>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411067 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?10683>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411067 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=506403>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411067 langual:B1067)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411067 "MANSFELD:7576")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411067 "PLANTS:CIAU7")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "Citrus aurantiifolia (Christm. & Panz.) Swingle")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "Citrus aurantiifolia (Christm.) Swingle")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "Citrus ×aurantiifolia (Christm.) Swingle (pro sp.)")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "citrus aurantiifolia"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "citrus medica var. acida"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "indian lime"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "key lime"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411067 "sour lime"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411067 "lime (citrus) plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411067 obo:FOODON_03411139)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411072 (sultana grape plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411072 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411072 "The sultana (also called the sultanina) is a type of white, seedless grape assumed to originate from the Turkish, Greek, or Iranian area. 
Unprocessed sultanas must be obtained from grapes of the varieties (cultivars) *Vitis vinifera* L. Apyrena.[http://eur-lex.europa.eu/LexUriServ/LexUriServ.do?uri=OJ:L:1999:192:0021:0032:EN:PDF]"@en)
