# Class: obo:FOODON_03411107 (pear tomato plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411107 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411107 "Pear tomato or teardrop tomato is the common name for any one in a group of indeterminate heirloom tomatoes. It originated in Europe in the 1700s. There are yellow, orange, and red varieties of this tomato; the yellow variety being most common. They are generally sweet, and are in the shape of a pear, but smaller.

Pear tomatoes are commonly eaten raw, but can also be used as a garnish, as an ingredient in many different dishes and sauces, or in drinks."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411107 "WIKIPEDIA:Pear_tomato")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411107 langual:B1107)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411107 "italian tomato"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411107 "lycopersicon lycopersicum var. pyriforme"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411107 "pear tomato plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411107 obo:NCBITaxon_4081)

