# Class: obo:FOODON_03411119 (pandalid shrimp family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411119 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411119 "The family *Pandalidae* is a taxon of caridean shrimp. These species are commonly called pandalid shrimp. They are edible and have high economic value. They are characterised by the subdivided carpus of the second pereiopod and, mainly, by the lack of the chelae (claws) on the first pereiopod. This is a cold-water family, and their representation in tropical areas is made by deep-sea shrimp. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandalidae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411119 <http://eol.org/pages/7176>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411119 langual:B1119)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411119 "pandalid shrimps"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411119 "pandalid shrimps nei"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411119 "pandalidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411119 "pink shrimps"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411119 "pandalid shrimp family"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411119 obo:FOODON_03411237)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411121 (bramble berry plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411121 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411121 "Rubus is a large and diverse genus of flowering plants in the rose family, *Rosaceae*, subfamily *Rosoideae*, with 250-700 species. Raspberries, blackberries, and dewberries are common, widely distributed members of the genus. Most of these plants have woody stems with prickles like roses; spines, bristles, and gland-tipped hairs are also common in the genus. The Rubus fruit, sometimes called a bramble fruit, is an aggregate of drupelets. The term \"cane fruit\" (or \"cane-fruit\") applies to any Rubus species or hybrid which is commonly grown with supports such as wires or canes, including raspberries, blackberries, and hybrids such as loganberry, boysenberry, marionberry and tayberry. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubus]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411121 <http://eol.org/pages/30108>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411121 langual:B1121)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411121 "rubus spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411121 "bramble berry plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411121 obo:FOODON_03411231)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411122 (marine mammal)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411122 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411122 "A mammal that is primarily ocean-dwelling or depends on the ocean for its food."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411122 "WIKIPEDIA:Marine_mammal")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000600 obo:FOODON_03411122 "Mammals originally evolved on land, but later marine mammals evolved to live back in the ocean. There are five groups of marine mammals: (1) Order Sirenia: the manatee, dugong, and sea cow. (2) Order Carnivora, family Ursidae: the polar bear. (3) Order Carnivora, infrafamily Pinnipedia: the seal, sea lion, and walrus. (4) Order Carnivora, family Mustelidae: the Sea Otter and Marine Otter. (5) Order Cetacea: the whale, dolphin, and porpoise."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411122 langual:B1122)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411122 "cetacea"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411122 "marine mammal"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411122 obo:FOODON_03411134)

