# Class: obo:FOODON_03411200 (cowpea plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411200 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411200 "The cowpea (*Vigna unguiculata*) is an annual herbaceous legume from the genus *Vigna. Due to its tolerance for sandy soil and low rainfall it is an important crop in the semi-arid regions across Africa and other countries. It requires very few inputs, as the plants root nodules are able to fix atmospheric nitrogen, making it a valuable crop for resource poor farmers and well-suited to intercropping with other crops. The whole plant is used as forage for animals, with its use as cattle feed likely responsible for its name. Four subspecies of cowpea are recognised, of which three are cultivated. Cultivated cowpeas are known by the common names black-eyed pea, southern pea, yardlong bean, catjang, and crowder pea.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cowpea]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411200 <http://eol.org/pages/655178>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411200 obo:NCBITaxon_3917)
