AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000600 obo:FOODON_03411223 "Mussel is the common name used for members of several families of bivalve molluscs, from saltwater and freshwater habitats. These groups have in common a shell whose outline is elongated and asymmetrical compared with other edible clams, which are often more or less rounded or oval."@en)
