# Class: obo:FOODON_03411275 (lemon plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411275 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411275 "The lemon, *Citrus limon *(L.) Osbeck, is a species of small evergreen tree in the flowering plant family Rutaceae, native to Asia. The tree's ellipsoidal yellow fruit is used for culinary and non-culinary purposes throughout the world, primarily for its juice, which has both culinary and cleaning uses. The pulp and rind (zest) are also used in cooking and baking. The juice of the lemon is about 5% to 6% citric acid, with a pH of around 2.2, giving it a sour taste. The distinctive sour taste of lemon juice makes it a key ingredient in drinks and foods such as lemonade and lemon meringue pie. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411275 <http://eol.org/pages/4414>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411275 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?10732>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411275 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=28885>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411275 langual:B1275)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411275 "MANSFELD:7625")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411275 "PLANTS:CILI5")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411275 "Citrus limon (L.) Burm. f.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411275 "Citrus limon (L.) Burm. fil.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411275 "Citrus ×limon (L.) Burm. f. (pro sp.)")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411275 "citrus limon"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411275 "citrus medica var. limonum"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411275 "lemon plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411275 obo:FOODON_03411139)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411275 obo:FOODON_03414168)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411276 (tomato plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411276 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411276 "The word \"tomato\" may refer to the plant (*Solanum lycopersicum*) or the edible, typically red, fruit that it bears. Originating in South America, the tomato was spread around the world following the Spanish colonization of the Americas, and its many varieties are now widely grown, often in greenhouses in cooler climates.See also the list of tomato cultivars"@en)
