# Class: obo:FOODON_03411312 (wheat plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411312 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411312 "Wheat (*Triticum* spp.) is a domesticated grass from the Levant that is cultivated worldwide. Major cultivated species of wheat:

    * Common wheat or Bread wheat (*Triticum aestivum*) A hexaploid species that is the most widely cultivated in the world.

    * Durum (*Triticum durum*) The only tetraploid form of wheat widely used today, and the second most widely cultivated wheat.

    * Einkorn (*Triticum monococcum*) A diploid species with wild and cultivated variants. Domesticated at the same time as emmer wheat, but never reached the same importance.

    * Emmer (*Triticum dicoccon*) A tetraploid species, cultivated in ancient times but no longer in widespread use.

    * Spelt (*Triticum spelta*) Another hexaploid species cultivated in limited quantities."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411312 "WIKIPEDIA:Wheat")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411312 langual:B1312)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411312 "triticum spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411312 "wheat plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411312 obo:FOODON_03411017)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411312 obo:FOODON_03411324)

