# Class: obo:FOODON_03411379 (field corn plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411379 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411379 "Field corn is maize of varieties that (in contrast with sweet corn and popcorn) are not, in the United States, grown primarily for consumption as human food in the form of fresh kernels. More than 98% of corn-growing land in the U.S. is in use for field-corn production. Principal field corn varieties are Dent corn, Flint corn, Flour corn (including blue corn (*Zea mays amylacea*), and Waxy corn."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411379 "WIKIPEDIA:Field_corn")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411379 <http://eol.org/pages/8223>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411379 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?311987>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411379 langual:B1379)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411379 "PLANTS:ZEMAM2")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "Zea mays L. ssp. mays")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "Zea mays L. subsp. mays")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "Zea mays ssp. mays L.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "corn, field"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "dent corn"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "flint corn"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "maize"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "podcorn"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "zea mays var. indentata (not acc.)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411379 "zea mays var. indurata (not acc.)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03411379 "Field corn is a general term used in North America for corn varieties other than sweet corn, popcorn, yellow food grade corn used for yellow corn meal or flour and corn starch, and white food-grade corn used for white meal or flour and corn starch. Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Field_corn

LanguaL curation note: Searching note--use 'field corn' for any breakfast cereal or snack food having 'corn' as the first ingredient."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411379 "field corn plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411379 obo:FOODON_00003425)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411379 obo:FOODON_03411012)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411379 obo:FOODON_03411016)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411379 obo:FOODON_03411017)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411380 (sweet corn plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411380 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411380 "Sweet corn (*Zea mays* convar. *saccharata* var. *rugosa*; also called Indian corn, sugar corn, and pole corn) is a variety of maize with a high sugar content. Sweet corn is the result of a naturally occurring recessive mutation in the genes which control conversion of sugar to starch inside the endosperm of the corn kernel. Unlike field corn varieties, which are harvested when the kernels are dry and mature (dent stage), sweet corn is picked when immature (milk stage) and prepared and eaten as a vegetable, rather than a grain. Since the process of maturation involves converting sugar to starch, sweet corn stores poorly and must be eaten fresh, canned, or frozen, before the kernels become tough and starchy."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411380 wikipedia:Sweet_corn)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411380 <http://eol.org/pages/1115259>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411380 obo:NCBITaxon_4577)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411380 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=42269>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411380 langual:B1380)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411380 "Zea mays L.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411380 "golden corn"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411380 "sugar corn"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411380 "sweet corn"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411380 "zea mays var. rugosa"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411380 "sweet corn plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411380 obo:FOODON_00003425)

