# Class: obo:FOODON_03411478 (scallion plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411478 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411478 "An edible plant of various *Allium* species, all of which are \"onion-like\", having hollow green leaves and lacking a fully developed root bulb."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411478 "WIKIPEDIA:Scallion")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411478 <http://eol.org/pages/8187>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411478 langual:B1478)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "green shallot"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "long onion"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "onion stick"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "salad onion"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "baby onion"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "gibbon"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "green onion"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "precious onions"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "spring onion"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "syboe"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411478 "yard onion"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03411478 "Scallions are also known as green onions, spring onions, salad onions, green shallots, onion sticks, long onions, baby onions, precious onions, yard onions, gibbons, or syboes.  The Welsh onion (*Allium fistulosum*) does not form bulbs even when mature, and is grown in the West almost exclusively as a scallion or salad onion, although in Asia this species is of primary importance and used both fresh and in cooking. \"Scallion\" is also used for young plants of the common onion (*Allium cepa* var. *cepa*) and shallot (*Allium cepa* var. *aggregatum*, formerly *Allium ascalonicum*), harvested before bulbs form, or sometimes when slight bulbing has occurred. Most of the cultivars grown in the West primarily as salad onions or scallions belong to *Allium cepa* var. *cepa*. Other species sometimes used as scallions include *Allium ×proliferum* and *Allium ×wakegi*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411478 "scallion plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:FOODON_03411478 <https://www.soscuisine.com/blog/knowing-the-difference-between-shallots-and-scallions/>)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411478 obo:FOODON_03411058)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411478 obo:FOODON_03414302)

