# Class: obo:FOODON_03411755 (Carangidae family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411755 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411755 "The Carangidae are a family of fish which includes the jacks, pompanos, jack mackerels, runners, and scads. They are marine fishes found in the Atlantic, Indian and Pacific Oceans. Most species are fast-swimming predatory fishes that hunt in the waters above reefs and in the open sea; some dig in the sea floor for invertebrates."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411755 <https://www.clovegarden.com/ingred/seafishv.html>)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000600 obo:FOODON_03411755 "Common names within family Carangidae are very disorderly, including Jacks, Amberjacks, Pompanos, Trevally, Bumpers and Scads, without clear deliniation as to which are which.[https://www.clovegarden.com/ingred/seafishv.html]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411755 <http://eol.org/pages/5361>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411755 langual:B1755)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411755 "jack family"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411755 "scad family"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411755 "carangidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411755 "Carangidae family"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411755 obo:FOODON_03411581)

