# Class: obo:FOODON_03412309 (snakehead family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412309 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412309 "The snakeheads are members of the freshwater perciform fish family *Channidae*, native to parts of Africa and Asia. These elongated, predatory fish are distinguished by their long dorsal fins, large mouths, and shiny teeth. They breathe air with gills, which allows them to migrate short distances over land. They are valuable as a food source and have become notorious as an intentionally released invasive species. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakehead_(fish)]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412309 <http://eol.org/pages/5349>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412309 langual:B2309)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412309 "channidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412309 "snakehead family"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412309 obo:FOODON_03411581)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412310 (betel plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412310 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412310 "The Betel (*Piper betle*) is a spice whose leaves have medicinal properties. The plant is evergreen and perennial, with glossy heart-shaped leaves and white catkins, and grows to a height of about 1 metre. The Betel plant originated in Malaysia and now grows in India, Indonesia and Sri Lanka. The best Betel leaf is the \"Magahi\" variety (literally from the Magadha region) grown near Patna in Bihar, India. The plant is known by a series of different names in the regions in which it is consumed - among these are Vetrilai (Tamil) (Source:"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03412310 "WIKIPEDIA:Betel).")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412310 langual:B2310)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412310 "betle pepper"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412310 "piper betle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412310 "betel plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412310 obo:FOODON_03413359)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412311 (betel nut palm plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412311 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412311 "Betel nut, also known as Pinang or Areca nut, is the seed of the Betel Palm (*Areca catechu*). Betel nuts are often chewed for their helpful effects, which are caused by the relatively high levels of alkaloids in the seed. Chewing betel nuts is an important and popular cultural activity in many Asian countries"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03412311 "WIKIPEDIA:Betel_nut")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412311 langual:B2311)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412311 "areca catechu"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412311 "betel nut palm plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412311 obo:FOODON_03413359)

