# Class: obo:FOODON_03412733 (mirabelle plum plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412733 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412733 "The mirabelle plum, also known as the mirabelle prune (*Prunus domestica* subsp. *syriaca*), is the edible drupaceous fruit of the mirabelle plum tree, a cultivar of the plum tree of the genus *Prunus*. 
 The mirabelle is identified by its small, oval shape, smooth-textured flesh, and especially by its red, or dark yellow colour which becomes flecked in appearance. They are known for being sweet and full of flavour. The fruit is primarily used in fruit preserves and dessert pies, and its juice is commonly fermented for wine or distilled into plum brandy. Ninety percent of mirabelle plums grown commercially are made into either jam (70%) or eau de vie (20%). The plums are also excellent when eaten fresh. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirabelle_plum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412733 <http://eol.org/pages/8097>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412733 langual:B2733)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412733 "MANSFELD:9350")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03412733 "Prunus domestica L. subsp. syriaca (Borkh.) Janch.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412733 "prunus domestica var. syriaca"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412733 "prunus insititia var. syriaca"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412733 "syrian plum"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412733 "mirabelle plum plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412733 obo:FOODON_03411662)

