# Class: obo:FOODON_03413684 (giant catfishes)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413684 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413684 "The shark catfishes form the family *Pangasiidae*. They are found in fresh and brackish waters across southern Asia, from Pakistan to Borneo. Among the 30-odd members of this family is the plant-eating, endangered Mekong giant catfish *Pangasianodon gigas*, one of the largest known freshwater fish. Several species are the basis of productive aquaculture industries in Vietnam's Mekong Delta. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_catfish]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413684 <http://eol.org/pages/5092>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413684 langual:B3684)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03413684 "pangasiidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03413684 "giant catfishes"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03413684 obo:FOODON_03411598)

