# Class: obo:FOODON_03413742 (plum tomato plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413742 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413742 "A plum tomato, also known as a processing tomato or paste tomato, is a type of tomato bred for sauce and packing purposes. Varieties commonly available in markets include Roma VF and San Marzano (semi-determinate; a signature tomato of Italian cuisine), though there are many other varieties, such as the short-season Ropreco Paste and the larger Amish Paste and Big Mama. Five hybrid cultivars grown in California constitute over 60% of total production of processing tomatoes. Small plum tomatoes (similar in size to cherry tomatoes) are known as grape tomatoes."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03413742 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_tomato"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://schema.org/image> obo:FOODON_03413742 "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Plum_Tomatoes%2C_Lexington_MA.jpg/320px-Plum_Tomatoes%2C_Lexington_MA.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413742 langual:B3742)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03413742 "grape tomato plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03413742 "roma tomato plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03413742 "plum tomato plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03413742 obo:NCBITaxon_4081)

