AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414166 "A large fowl, one of the two species in the genus Meleagris and the same as the wild turkey. [...] all of the main domestic turkey varieties today descend from the turkey raised in central Mexico that was subsequently imported into Europe by the Spanish in the 16th century."@en)
