# Class: obo:FOODON_03414346 (tucum plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414346 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414346 "Astrocaryum vulgare (common names Tucum or Tucumã-do-Pará in Brazil, Aouara in French Guiana, Wara awara in Guyana, awarra in Suriname, Chontilla in Ecuador) is a palm native to Amazon Rainforest vegetation, typical of the Pará state in Brazil. This plant has edible fruit, which are also used for biodiesel production. This plant is cited in Flora Brasiliensis by Carl Friedrich Philipp von Martius.[]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414346 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?5941>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414346 langual:B4346)
