# Class: obo:FOODON_03414458 (advantame)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414458 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414458 "Advantame is a new ultrahigh potency sweetener and flavor enhancer derived from aspartame and vanillin."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414458 <https://caloriecontrol.org/sugar-substitutes/>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414458 langual:B4458)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03414458 "\"Advantame is approximately 20,000 times sweeter than sugar and 100 times sweeter than aspartame.\" [https://caloriecontrol.org/sugar-substitutes/]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414458 "advantame"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414458 obo:FOODON_00001618)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414459 (cucumis species)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414459 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414459 "Cucumis is a genus of twining, tendril-bearing plants in the *Cucurbitaceae* family which includes the cucumber (*Cucumis sativus*), muskmelons (*Cucumis melo*, including cantaloupe and honeydew), the horned melon (*Cucumis metuliferus*), and the West Indian gherkin (*Cucumis anguria*). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumis]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414459 langual:B4459)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414459 "cucumis species"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414459 obo:FOODON_03414460)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414460 (gourd/squash family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414460 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414460 "The *Cucurbitaceae*, also called cucurbits and the gourd family, are a plant family consisting of about 965 species in around 95 genera, the most important of which are: 
  *Cucurbita* - squash, pumpkin, zucchini, some gourds; 
  *Lagenaria* - calabash, and others that are inedible; 
  *Citrullus* - watermelon (*C. lanatus, C. colocynthis*) and others; 
  *Cucumis* - cucumber (*C. sativus*), various melons; 
  *Luffa* - luffa, loofah"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414460 wikipedia:Cucurbitaceae)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414460 langual:B4460)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414460 "cucurbitaceae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414460 "gourd/squash family"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414460 obo:FOODON_03413357)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414466 (tunicate)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414466 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414466 "Tunicates, previously known as *Urochordata* or urochordates, are members of the *Tunicata*, a subphylum of the phylum *Chordata*. They are marine filter feeders with a saclike morphology. In their respiration and feeding they take in water through an incurrent (or inhalant) siphon and expel the filtered water through an excurrent (or exhalant) siphon. Most adult tunicates are sessile and attached to rocks or similarly suitable surfaces on the ocean floor; others such as salps, doliolids and pyrosomes swim in the pelagic zone as adults. Various species are commonly known as sea squirts or sea pork."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414466 "WIKIPEDIA:Tunicate")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414466 langual:B4466)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414466 "oopah"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414466 "sea squirt"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414466 "tunicata"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414466 "tunicate"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414466 obo:FOODON_00002581)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414467 (ascidian)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414467 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414467 "Ascidiacea (commonly known as the ascidians or sea squirts) is a class in the Tunicata subphylum of sac-like marine invertebrate filter feeders. Ascidians are characterized by a tough outer \"tunic\" made of the polysaccharide tunicin, as compared to other tunicates which are less rigid."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414467 "WIKIPEDIA:Ascidiacea")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414467 <http://eol.org/pages/1486>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414467 langual:B4467)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414467 "ascidiacea"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414467 "sea squirts"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414467 "ascidian"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414467 obo:FOODON_03414466)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414470 (brown bear)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414470 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414470 "The brown bear (*Ursus arctos*) is a large bear distributed across much of northern Eurasia and North America. Adult bears generally weigh between 100 and 635 kg (220 and 1,400 lb) and its largest subspecies, the Kodiak bear, rivals the polar bear as the largest member of the bear family and as the largest land-based predator. There are several recognized subspecies within the brown bear species. In North America, two types are generally recognized, the coastal brown bear and the inland grizzly bear, and the two types could broadly define all brown bear subspecies."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414470 "WIKIPEDIA:Brown_bear")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414470 <http://eol.org/pages/328581>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414470 obo:NCBITaxon_9644)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414470 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=180543>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414470 langual:B4470)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414470 "MSW3:14000970")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03414470 "Ursus arctos Linnaeus, 1758")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414470 "ursus arctos"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414470 "brown bear"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414470 obo:FOODON_03412406)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414470 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9644))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414471 (kodiak bear)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414471 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414471 "The Kodiak bear (*Ursus arctos middendorffi*), also known as the Kodiak brown bear or the Alaskan grizzly bear or American brown bear, occupies the islands of the Kodiak Archipelago in South-Western Alaska. Its name in the Alutiiq language is Taquka-aq. It is the largest subspecies of brown bear."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414471 "WIKIPEDIA:Kodiak_Bear")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414471 <http://eol.org/pages/7664>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414471 langual:B4471)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414471 "MSW3:14000982")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03414471 "Ursus arctos middendorffi Merriam, 1896")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414471 "taquka-aq"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414471 "ursus arctos middendorffi"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414471 "kodiak bear"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414471 obo:FOODON_03414470)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414472 (grizzly bear)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414472 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414472 "The grizzly bear (*Ursus arctos horribilis*), also known as the silvertip bear, the grizzly, or the North American brown bear, is a subspecies of brown bear (Ursus arctos) that generally lives in the uplands of western North America. This subspecies is thought to descend from Ussuri brown bears which crossed to Alaska from eastern Russia 100,000 years ago, though they did not move south until 13,000 years ago."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414472 "WIKIPEDIA:Grizzly_bear")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414472 <http://eol.org/pages/7664>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414472 langual:B4472)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414472 "MSW3:14000979")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03414472 "Ursus arctos horribilis Ord, 1815")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414472 "grizzly"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414472 "north american brown bear"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414472 "silvertip bear"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414472 "ursus arctos horribilis"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414472 "grizzly bear"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414472 obo:FOODON_03414470)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414473 (california golden bear)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414473 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414473 "The California golden bear or California grizzly (*Ursus arctos californicus*) is an extinct subspecies of the brown bear. The California golden bear disappeared from the state of California in 1922, when the last one was shot in Tulare County. In 1866, a grizzly weighing 2,200 pounds was killed in Valley Center, California, the largest grizzly killed in California."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414473 "WIKIPEDIA:California_golden_bear")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414473 <http://eol.org/pages/7664>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414473 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=726987>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414473 langual:B4473)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414473 "MSW3:14000974")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03414473 "Ursus arctos californicus Merriam, 1896")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414473 "ursus arctos californicus"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414473 "california golden bear"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414473 obo:FOODON_03412406)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414476 (polyplacophoran)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414476 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414476 "Chitons are small to large marine molluscs in the class *Polyplacophora*, which formerly was known as *Amphineura*. There are approximately 940 extant and 430 fossil species recognized. These molluscs are also sometimes commonly known as sea cradles or \"coat-of-mail shells\". They are also sometimes referred to more formally as loricates, polyplacophorans, and rarely as polyplacophores. Chitons have a dorsal shell which is composed of eight separate shell plates or valves. These plates overlap somewhat at the front and back edges, and yet the plates articulate well with one another."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414476 "WIKIPEDIA:Polyplacophora")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414476 <http://eol.org/pages/2680>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414476 langual:B4476)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414476 "amphineura"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414476 "chiton"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414476 "chíton"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414476 "loricate"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414476 "polplacophore"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414476 "polyplacophora"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414476 "polyplacophoran"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414476 obo:FOODON_03412112)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414479 (white-winged scoter)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414479 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414479 "The White-winged Scoter (*Melanitta deglandi* or *Melanitta fusca deglandi*) is a large sea duck."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414479 "WIKIPEDIA:White-winged_scoter")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414479 <http://eol.org/pages/8027>)
