# Class: obo:FOODON_03414546 (caju-docerrado plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414546 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414546 "Anacardium othonianum is a tree native from the tropical savanna (cerrado) region of Brazil, whose fruit is similar to (but smaller than) that of the common cashew tree (*Anacardium occidentale*) of the Brazilian Northeast. It is locally known by the Tupi-derived name cajuí, and by the Portuguese names caju-de-árvore-do-cerrado (\"tree cashew of the cerrado\"),[1] caju-vermelho-de-goiás (\"red cashew from Goiás\"),[2] cajuzinho-do-cerrado or just cajuzinho (\"little cashew\"). Anacardium othonianum Rizzini [The Plant List, KEW-2635918]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414546 "WIKIPEDIA:Anacardium_othonianum")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414546 langual:B4546)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414546 "anacardium othonianum"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414546 "caju-de-árvore-do-cerrado"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414546 "cajuzinho"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414546 "cajuzinho-do-cerrado"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414546 "cajuí"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414546 "little cashew"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414546 "caju-docerrado plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414546 obo:FOODON_03411024)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414556 (rhea)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414556 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414556 "The rheas are large ratites (flightless birds without a keel on their sternum bone) in the order *Rheiformes*, native to South America, related to the ostrich and emu. There are two extant species: the greater or American rhea and the lesser or Darwin's rhea."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414556 "WIKIPEDIA:Rhea_(bird)")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414556 langual:B4556)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414556 "pterocnemia pennata"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414556 "rhea americana"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414556 "rheidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414556 "rhea"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414556 obo:FOODON_03414362)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414559 (fish, osteoglossiform)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414559 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414559 "Osteoglossiformes (Greek: \"bony tongues\") is a relatively primitive order of ray-finned fish that contains two sub-orders, the *Osteoglossoidei* and the *Notopteroidei*. All of at least 245 living species inhabit freshwater. They are found in South America, Africa, Australia and southern Asia, having first evolved in Gondwana before that continent broke up. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osteoglossiformes]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414559 <http://eol.org/pages/5386>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414559 langual:B4559)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414559 "bonytongues"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414559 "osteoglossiformes"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414559 "fish, osteoglossiform"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414559 obo:FOODON_03411365)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414560 (mooneye family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414560 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414560 "The mooneyes are a family, the *Hiodontidae*, of ray-finned fish comprising two living and three extinct species in the genus *Hiodon*. They are large-eyed, fork-tailed fish that physically resemble shads. Their common name comes from the metallic gold or silver shine of their eyes. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mooneye]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414560 <http://eol.org/pages/5386>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414560 langual:B4560)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414560 "hiodontidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414560 "mooneye"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414560 "mooneye family"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414560 obo:FOODON_03414559)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414565 (fulmar)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414565 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414565 "The fulmars are tubenosed seabirds of the family *Procellariidae*. The family consists of two extant species and two extinct fossils from the Miocene.</br>The northern fulmar (*Fulmarus glacialis*) or just fulmar lives in the North Atlantic and North Pacific, whereas the southern fulmar, (*Fulmarus glacialoides*) is, as its name implies, a bird of the Southern Ocean. Fulmars superficially resemble gulls, but are readily distinguished by their flight on stiff wings, and their tube noses. They breed on cliffs, laying a single egg on a ledge of bare rock. Outside the breeding season, they are pelagic, feeding on fish, squid and shrimp in the open ocean."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414565 "WIKIPEDIA:Fulmar")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414565 <http://eol.org/pages/19855>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414565 langual:B4565)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414565 "fulmarus spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414565 "fulmar"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414565 obo:FOODON_00002616)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414571 (minke whale)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414571 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414571 "Balaenoptera, from the Latin *balaena* (whale) and *pteron* (fin), is a genus of *Balaenopteridae*, the rorquals, and contains eight extant species. The species *Balaenoptera omurai* was published in 2003. *Balaenoptera* is the most diverse genus of its family, the only other member being the Humpback Whale, *Megaptera novaeangliae*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414571 "WIKIPEDIA:Balaenoptera")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414571 <http://eol.org/pages/7660>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414571 langual:B4571)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414571 "balaenoptera spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414571 "baleen whale"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414571 "finback whale"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414571 "rorquals"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414571 "minke whale"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414571 obo:FOODON_03411343)

