# Class: obo:FOODON_03414693 (drooping mistletoe plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414693 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414693 "Amyema pendula, also known as drooping mistletoe or furry drooping mistletoe, is a species of flowering plant, an epiphytic hemiparasitic plant of the family *Loranthaceae*, found attached to several species of Australian eucalypt and occasionally on some species of Acacia.[]"@en)
