# Class: obo:FOODON_03414729 (cattail plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414729 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414729 "Typha is a genus of about 30 species of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family *Typhaceae*. These plants have many common names. They may be known in British English as bulrush, or reedmace, in American English as cattail, punks, or corn dog grass, in Australia as cumbungi or bulrush, in Canada as bulrush or cattail, and in New Zealand as raupõ. The rhizomes are edible. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typha]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414729 <http://eol.org/pages/66364>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414729 langual:B4729)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414729 "bulrush"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414729 "corn dog grass"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414729 "cumbungi"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414729 "punks"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414729 "typha spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414729 "cattail plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414729 obo:FOODON_03411058)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414730 (orchid plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414730 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414730 "The *Orchidaceae* are a diverse and widespread family of flowering plants, with blooms that are often colourful and often fragrant, commonly known as the orchid family. The *Orchidaceae* have about 28,000 currently accepted species, distributed in about 763 genera. The largest genera are *Bulbophyllum* (2,000 species), *Epidendrum* (1,500 species), *Dendrobium* (1,400 species) and *Pleurothallis* (1,000 species). The family also includes *Vanilla* (the genus of the vanilla plant), *Orchis* (type genus), and many commonly cultivated plants such as *Phalaenopsis* and *Cattleya*. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchidaceae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414730 <http://eol.org/pages/8156>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414730 langual:B4730)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414730 "orchidaceae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414730 "orchid plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414730 obo:FOODON_03411058)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414731 (dainty-bird orchid plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414731 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414731 "Chiloglottis is a small genus in the orchid family *Orchidaceae*. This genus of deciduous, terrestrial orchids is indigenous to Australia and New Zealand (including Chatham Island and the Antipodes). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiloglottis]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414731 <http://eol.org/pages/8156>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414731 langual:B4731)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414731 "chiloglottis spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414731 "dainty-bird orchid plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414731 obo:FOODON_03414730)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414732 (boat orchid plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414732 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414732 "Cymbidium, or boat orchid, is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the orchid family *Orchidaceae*. The species *Cymbidium hookerianum* is considered a delicacy in Bhutan where it is traditionally cooked in a spicy curry or stew and called \"olatshe\" or \"olachoto\". [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cymbidium]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414732 <http://eol.org/pages/21177>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414732 langual:B4732)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414732 "cymbidium spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414732 "boat orchid plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414732 obo:FOODON_03414730)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414733 (king orchid plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414733 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414733 "Dendrobium speciosum is not only a widespread Australian orchid but also a very variable orchid, forming a species complex. It is known under several common names: outstanding dendrobium, king orchid, and the somewhat misleading rock lily. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dendrobium_speciosum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414733 <http://eol.org/pages/8156>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414733 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?410954>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414733 langual:B4733)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03414733 "Dendrobium speciosum Sm.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414733 "dendrobium speciosum"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414733 "rock lily"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414733 "utstanding dendrobium"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414733 "king orchid plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414733 obo:FOODON_03414730)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414734 (potato orchid plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414734 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414734 "Gastrodia sesamoides R.Br. Is a saprophyte in the Orchid family. Common names include Potato Orchid, Native Potato, Bell Orchid and Cinnamon Bells. The Potato Orchid is found in Australia and New Zealand. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastrodia_sesamoides]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414734 <http://eol.org/pages/8156>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414734 langual:B4734)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414734 "bell orchid"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414734 "cinnamon bells"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414734 "gastrodia spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414734 "native potato"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414734 "potato orchid plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414734 obo:FOODON_03414730)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414735 (greenhood orchid plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414735 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414735 "Pterostylis is a genus of about 120 species of plants in the orchid family, *Orchidaceae*. Commonly called greenhood orchids, they are terrestrial, deciduous, perennial, tuberous, herbs found in Australia, New Zealand, New Guinea, New Caledonia and one Indonesian island. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pterostylis]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414735 <http://eol.org/pages/8156>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414735 langual:B4735)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414735 "pterostylis spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414735 "greenhood orchid plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414735 obo:FOODON_03414730)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414736 (lovegrass plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414736 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414736 "Eragrostis is large and widespread genus of plants in the grass family, found in many countries on all inhabited continents and many islands. *Eragrostis* is commonly known as lovegrass or canegrass. Lovegrass is commonly used as livestock fodder. The seeds appear to be of high nutritional value for some animals, but they are also very tiny and collecting them for human food is cumbersome and hence uncommon. A notable exception is teff (*Eragrostis tef*), which is used to make traditional breads on the Horn of Africa. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eragrostis]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414736 <http://eol.org/pages/108048>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414736 langual:B4736)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414736 "canegrass"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414736 "eragrostid spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414736 "lovegrass plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414736 obo:FOODON_03413378)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414737 (signalgrass plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414737 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414737 "Brachiaria, or signalgrass, is a genus of plants in the grass family native to tropical and subtropical regions of Asia, Africa, Australia, southern Europe, the Americas, and various islands. There are over 100 species. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brachiaria]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414737 <http://eol.org/pages/108119>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414737 langual:B4737)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414737 "brachiaria spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414737 "signalgrass plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414737 obo:FOODON_03413378)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414738 (tanglehead plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414738 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414738 "Heteropogon is a genus of annual and perennial plants in the grass family known generally as tangleheads, widespread primarily in tropical and subtropical regions. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heteropogon]"@en)
