# Class: obo:FOODON_03414758 (costus plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414758 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414758 "Costus is a group of perennial herbaceous plants in the family (*Costaceae*) described by Linnaeus as a genus in 1753. It is widespread through tropical and subtropical regions of Asia, Africa, and the Americas. Costus is often characterized and distinguished from relatives such as *Zingiber* (true ginger) by its spiraling stems. The genus as a whole is thus often called spiral gingers. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costus]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414758 <http://eol.org/pages/37906>)
