AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414762 "Dendrocnide is a genus of 37 species of shrubs to large trees in the nettle family *Urticaceae*. They have a wide distribution across Southeast Asia, North East India, Australia and the Pacific Islands. They are colloquially known as stinging trees, stinging nettles or nettle trees. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dendrocnide]"@en)
