# Class: obo:FOODON_03414899 (terrestrial invertebrate)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414899 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414899 "Invertebrates are animals that neither possess nor develop a vertebral column (commonly known as a backbone or spine), derived from the notochord. This includes all animals apart from the subphylum *Vertebrata*. Familiar examples of invertebrates include insects; crabs, lobsters and their kin; snails, clams, octopuses and their kin; starfish, sea-urchins and their kin; jellyfish, and worms. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invertebrate] 
 Terrestrial invertebrates include ants, flies, crickets, grasshoppers and spiders. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrestrial_animal]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414899 langual:B4899)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414899 "insect"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414899 "invertebrate, land"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414899 "land snail"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414899 "terrestrial invertebrate"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414899 obo:FOODON_00002452)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414901 (arachnid)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414901 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414901 "Arachnids are a class (Arachnida) of joint-legged invertebrate animals (arthropods), in the subphylum *Chelicerata*. All arachnids have eight legs, although the front pair of legs in some species has converted to a sensory function, while in other species, different appendages can grow large enough to take on the appearance of extra pairs of legs. Spiders are the largest order in the class, which also includes scorpions, ticks, mites, harvestmen, and solifuges [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arachnid]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414901 langual:B4901)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03414901 "Arachnida")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414901 "arachnida"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414901 "arachnid"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414901 obo:FOODON_03414899)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414902 (earthworm)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414902 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414902 "An earthworm is a tube-shaped, segmented worm found in the phylum *Annelida*. Earthworms are commonly found living in soil, feeding on live and dead organic matter. Larger terrestrial earthworms are also called megadriles (which translates to \"big worms\"), as opposed to the microdriles (\"small worms\") in the semiaquatic families Tubificidae, Lumbricidae, and Enchytraeidae, among others. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthworm]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414902 langual:B4902)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414902 "annelida"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414902 "earthworm"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414902 obo:FOODON_03414899)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414903 (shads)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414903 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414903 "The *Alosinae*, or the shads, are a subfamily of fishes in the herring family *Clupeidae*. The subfamily comprises seven genera worldwide, and about 30 species. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alosinae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414903 <http://eol.org/pages/2777156>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414903 langual:B4903)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414903 "alosinae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414903 "shads"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414903 obo:FOODON_03411124)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414904 (helicidae)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414904 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414904 "Helicidae is a large, diverse family of small to large, air-breathing land snails, sometimes called the \"typical snails.\"  A number of species in this family are valued as food items, including *Cornu aspersum* (formerly *Helix aspersa*) the brown or garden snail, and *Helix pomatia* the \"escargot\""@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:FOODON_03414904 "Damion Dooley")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414904 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helicidae"@en)
