# Class: obo:FOODON_03480010 (packed in vinegar with sugar)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03480010 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03480010 "A mixture of vinegar and sugar which are used as a packing medium for food material."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03480010 langual:K0010)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03480010 "In the U.S., grain strength is calculated as 10 times the acid content expressed as acetic acid.  For example, 40 grain vinegar = 4% acetic acid; 120 grain vinegar = 12% acetic acid. [Technically Speaking about Vinegar - A food technologist's guide to vinegar, The Vinegar Institute, 5775 Peachtree-Dunwoody Road, Atlanta, Georgia 30342, USA].
LanguaL curation note: Used for sweetened vinegar-water mixture with grain of at least 10. For lower grain, use *PACKED IN SWEETENED LIQUID*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03480010 "packed in vinegar with sugar"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03480010 obo:FOODON_03480029)

