# Class: obo:FOODON_03510033 (low energy food claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510033 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510033 "A claim that a food is low in energy, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product does not contain more than 40 kcal (170 kJ)/100 g for solids or more than 20 kcal (80 kJ)/100 ml for liquids. For table-top sweeteners the limit of 4 kcal (17 kJ)/portion, with equivalent sweetening properties to 6 g of sucrose (approximately 1 teaspoon of sucrose), applies [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having 40 calories or less per amount customarily consumed (and per 50 grams of food if the amount customarily consumed is small). Meals and main dishes contain 120 calories or less per 100 grams of food [US FDA]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510033 langual:P0033)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510033 "low calorie food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03510033 "LanguaL curation note: Renamed from *LOW CALORIE FOOD* [LanguaL 2008]."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510033 "low energy food claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510033 obo:FOODON_03510066)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510033 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:IAO_0000136 obo:FOODON_03315839))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510034 (reduced energy food claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510034 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510034 "A claim that a food is energy-reduced, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the energy value is reduced by at least 30 %, with an indication of the characteristic(s) which make(s) the
food reduced in its total energy value [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having at least 25% fewer calories per amount customarily consumed from the calories of a comparable food product. The complarable food may not be 'low calorie' [US FDA]."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510034 langual:P0034)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510034 "reduced calorie food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03510034 "LanguaL curation note: Renamed from *REDUCED CALORIE FOOD* [LanguaL 2008]."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510034 "reduced energy food claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510034 obo:FOODON_03510066)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510034 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:IAO_0000136 obo:FOODON_03301413))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510035 (salt or sodium free claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510035 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510035 "A claim that a food is sodium-free or salt-free, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product contains no more than 0,005 g of sodium, or the equivalent value for salt, per 100 g. [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having less than 5 milligrams of salt or sodium per amount customarily consumed (or for meals and main dishes, less than 5 miligrams of salt or sodium per labeled serving). Such foods must not contain an ingredient that is salt or sodium or generally understood to comtain salt or sodium except where the ingredient listed is footnoted '*adds a trivial amount of {salt or sodium}' [US FDA]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510035 langual:P0035)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510035 "sodium or salt free food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510035 "salt or sodium free claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510035 obo:FOODON_03510077)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510036 (very low salt or sodium claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510036 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510036 "A claim that a food is very low in sodium/salt, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product contains no more than 0,04 g of sodium, or the equivalent value for salt, per 100 g or per 100 ml. This claim shall not be used for natural mineral waters and other waters [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having 35 milligrams or less salt or sodium per amount customarily consumed (and per 50 grams if the amount customarily consumed is small). Meals and main dishes contain 35 milligrams or less salt or sodium per 100 grams of food [US FDA]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510036 langual:P0036)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510036 "very low sodium or salt food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510036 "very low salt or sodium claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510036 obo:FOODON_03510077)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510037 (reduced salt or sodium claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510037 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510037 langual:P0037)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510037 "reduced sodium or salt food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510037 "reduced salt or sodium claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510037 obo:FOODON_03510077)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510038 (low salt or sodium claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510038 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510038 "A claim that a food is low in sodium/salt, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product contains no more than 0,12 g of sodium, or the equivalent value for salt, per 100 g or per 100 ml. For waters, other than natural mineral waters falling within the scope of Directive 80/777/EEC, this value should not exceed 2 mg of sodium per 100 ml [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having 140 milligrams or less salt or sodium per amount customarily consumed. Meals and main dishes have 140 milligrams or less salt or sodium per 100 grams food [US FDA]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510038 langual:P0038)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510038 "low sodium or salt food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510038 "low salt or sodium claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510038 obo:FOODON_03510077)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510039 (low fat food)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510039 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510039 "A claim that a food is low in fat, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product contains no more than 3 g of fat per 100 g for solids or 1,5 g of fat per 100 ml for liquids (1,8 g of fat per 100 ml for semi-skimmed milk). [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having 3 grams of fat or less per amount customarily consumed (and per 50 grams of food if the amount customarily consumed is small). Meals and main dishes contain 3 grams or less fat per 100 grams of food and not more than 30% of calories from fat [US FDA]."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510039 langual:P0039)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510039 "low fat food"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510039 obo:FOODON_03510069)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510040 (reduced fat food)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510040 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510040 "Food containing at least 25% less fat per amount customarily consumed from the fat content of a comparable food product. The comparable food may not be 'low fat'."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510040 langual:P0040)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510040 "reduced fat food"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510040 obo:FOODON_03510069)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510041 (cholesterol special claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510041 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510041 "All narrower term definitions extracted from 58 Federal Register 2302, January 6, 1993, part 101.62(d)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510041 langual:P0041)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510041 "cholesterol special claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510041 obo:FOODON_03510065)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510042 (cholesterol free claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510042 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510042 "Food having less than 2 milligrams cholesterol per amount customarily consumed (or for meals and main dishes, less than 2 milligrams cholesterol per labeled serving). Such food must contain no ingredient that contains cholesterol except where the ingredient listed has been footnoted '*adds a trivial amount of cholesterol'. If the food contains less than 2 milligrams cholesterol per amount customarily consumed by special processing and the total fat exceeds 13 grams cholesterol per amount or labeled serving, the amount of cholesterol must be 'Substantially less' (25%) than in a comparable food with significant market share (5% of market)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510042 langual:P0042)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510042 "no cholesterol food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510042 "cholesterol free claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510042 obo:FOODON_03510149)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510043 (low in cholesterol claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510043 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510043 "Food having 20 miligrams or less cholesterol per amount customarily consumed (and per 50 grams of food if the amount customarily consumed is small). Meals and main dishes contain 20 milligrams or less cholesterol per 100 grams of food. If the food qualifies by special processing and total fat exceeds 13 grams per amount and labeled serving, the amount of cholesterol must be 'substantially less' (25%) than in a comparable food with significant market share (5% of market)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510043 langual:P0043)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510043 "low in cholesterol claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510043 obo:FOODON_03510149)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510044 (reduced cholesterol claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510044 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510044 "Food having at least 25% less cholesterol per amount customarily consumed from the cholesterol content of a comparable food product. The comparable food may not be 'low cholesterol'."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510044 langual:P0044)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510044 "reduced cholesterol claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510044 obo:FOODON_03510149)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510045 (energy special claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510045 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510045 "All narrower term definitions are extracted from 58 Federal Register 2302, January 6, 1993, part 101.60(b) and from Corrigendum to Regulation (EC) No 1924/2006 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20 December 2006 on nutrition and health claims made on foods."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510045 langual:P0045)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510045 "calorie special claim or use"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03510045 "LanguaL curation note: Renamed from *CALORIE SPECIAL CLAIM OR USE*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510045 "energy special claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510045 obo:FOODON_03510065)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510047 (salt or sodium special claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510047 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510047 "All narrower term definitions extracted from 58 Federal Register 2032, January 6, 1993, part 101.61."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510047 langual:P0047)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510047 "sodium or salt special diet"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510047 "salt or sodium special claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510047 obo:FOODON_03510065)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510048 (high fiber food)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510048 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510048 "A claim that a food is high in fibre, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product contains at least 6 g of fibre per 100 g or at least 3 g of fibre per 100 kcal [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food that is promoted as a source of or as high in dietary fiber (often called simply 'fiber')."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510048 langual:P0048)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510048 "high dietary fiber food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510048 "high fiber food"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510048 obo:FOODON_03510049)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510049 (fiber special claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510049 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510049 "Food that is promoted as being either high or low in dietary fiber (often called simply 'fiber'). If the food is not low in total fat, total fat must be stated in conjunction with claim such as 'more fiber'."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510049 langual:P0049)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510049 "dietary fiber special claim or use"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510049 "fiber special claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510049 obo:FOODON_03510065)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510054 (fat free food)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510054 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510054 "A claim that a food is fat-free, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product contains no more than 0,5 g of fat per 100 g or 100 ml. However, claims expressed as \"X % fat-free\" shall be prohibited [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum].

Food having less than 0.5 grams fat per amount customarily consumed. Meals and main dishes have less than 0.5 grams fat per labeled serving. Such foods must contain no ingredient that is fat or understood to contain fat except when the ingredient listed has been footnoted '*adds a trivial amount of fat'."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510054 langual:P0054)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510054 "no fat food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510054 "nonfat food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510054 "fat free food"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510054 obo:FOODON_03510069)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510055 (energy free food claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510055 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510055 "A claim that a food is energy-free, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product does not contain more than 4 kcal (17 kJ)/100 ml. For table-top sweeteners the limit of 0.4 kcal (1.7 kJ)/portion, with equivalent sweetening properties to 6 g of sucrose (approximately 1 teaspoon of sucrose), applies [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having less than 5 calories per amount customarily consumed. Calorie amount is not defined for meals or main dishes [US FDA]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510055 langual:P0055)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510055 "calorie free food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03510055 "LanguaL curation note: Renamed from *CALORIE FREE FOOD* [LanguaL 2008]."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510055 "energy free food claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510055 obo:FOODON_03510066)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510056 (sugars free food)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510056 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510056 "A claim that a food is sugars-free, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made where the product contains no more than 0,5 g of sugars per 100 g or 100 ml [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having less than 0.5 grams sugars per amount customarily consumed (or for meals and main dishes, less than 0.5 grams sugars per labeled serving). Such foods nust contain no ingredient that is a sugar or generally understood to contain sugars except where the ingredient listed is footnoted '*adds a trivial amount of sugars' [US FDA]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510056 langual:P0056)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510056 "sugar free food"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510056 "sugars free food"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510056 obo:FOODON_03510091)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510057 (low in saturated fat food)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510057 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03510057 "A claim that a food is low in saturated fat, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer, may only be made if the sum of saturated fatty acids and trans-fatty acids in the product does not exceed 1.5 g per 100 g for solids or 0.75 g/100 ml for liquids and in either case the sum of saturated fatty acids and trans-fatty acids must not provide more than 10 % of energy. [REGULATION (EC) No 1924/2006 Corrigendum 2007-01-18].

Food having one gram or less saturated fat per amount customarily consumed and 15% or less of calories from saturated fat. Meals and main dishes contain one gram or less saturated fat per 100 grams food and less than 10% of calories from saturated fat."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510057 langual:P0057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510057 "low in saturated fat food"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510057 obo:FOODON_03510071)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03510059 (general label claim)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03510059 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03510059 langual:P0059)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03510059 "label claim"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03510059 "LanguaL curation note: Renamed from *LABEL CLAIM* [LanguaL 2008].

Use when any 'claim or use' index term is derived from either the food name appearing on the label or from information appearing on the label that is separate from the food name."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03510059 "general label claim"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03510059 obo:FOODON_03602001)

