# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_1081552 (Galeopsis segetum)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_1081552 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_1081552 "*Galeopsis segetum*, commonly known as Downy Hemp-nettle, is a species of flowering plant in the sage family, *Lamiaceae*. It grows as a weed in arable ground throughout Europe. Although superficially resembling the Stinging nettle it is of a different family and does not sting. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galeopsis_segetum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_1081552 "downy hemp-nettle plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_1081552 <http://eol.org/pages/483184>)
