# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_112823 (Pangium edule)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_112823 "*Pangium edule* (Indonesian: keluak or keluwak;Malay: kepayang) is a tall tree native to the mangrove swamps of Southeast Asia (Indonesia, Malaysia and Papua New Guinea). It produces a large poisonous fruit (the \"football fruit\") which can be made edible by fermentation. In Singapore and Malaysia, the seeds are best known as an essential ingredient in ayam (chicken) or babi (pork) buah keluak, a mainstay of Peranakan cuisine. Alternatively, the kernels may be ground up to form a thick black gravy called rawan (or rawon in parts of Indonesia)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_112823 "WIKIPEDIA:Pangium_edule")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_112823 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?26427>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_112823 langual:B4496)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_112823 "PLANTS:PAED4")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_112823 "Pangium edule Reinw.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_112823 "rowal"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:NCBITaxon_112823 obo:FOODON_03411174)

# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_112863 (Lycium barbarum)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_112863 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_112863 "Lycium barbarum varietal of Wolfberry, commercially called goji berry, is the common name for the fruit of two very closely related species: *Lycium barbarum* and *Lycium chinense*, two species of boxthorn in the family *Solanaceae* (which also includes the potato, tomato, eggplant, deadly nightshade, chili pepper, and tobacco). It is native to southeastern Europe and Asia."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_112863 "wolfberry plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_112863 "WIKIPEDIA:Lycium_chinense")
