# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_13393 (Cananga odorata)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_13393 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_13393 "*Cananga odorata*, known as the cananga tree, is a tropical tree that originates in Indonesia, which in the early 19th century spread to Malaysia and the Philippines. It is valued for the perfume extracted from its flowers, called ylang-ylang (a name also sometimes used for the tree itself), which is an essential oil used in aromatherapy. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cananga_odorata]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_13393 "ylang-ylang plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13393 <http://eol.org/pages/304899>)
