# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_13451 (Corylus avellana)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_13451 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_13451 "*Corylus avellana*, the common hazel, is a species of hazel native to Europe and western Asia. Common hazel is cultivated for its nuts. The name hazelnut applies to the nuts of any of the species of the genus *Corylus*. This hazelnut or cob nut, the kernel of the seed, is edible and used raw or roasted, or ground into a paste. The cob is round, compared with the longer filbert nut. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corylus_avellana]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_13451 "common hazel plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13451 <http://eol.org/pages/1147599>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13451 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?11643>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13451 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=501642>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13451 langual:B5022)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13451 "PLANTS:COAV80")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_13451 "Corylus avellana L.")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_13451 "cobnut"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_13451 "corylus avellana"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:NCBITaxon_13451 obo:FOODON_03411533)

# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_13452 (Corylus cornuta)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_13452 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "*Corylus cornuta* Marsh. is a deciduous shrubby hazel found in most of North America, from southern Canada south to Georgia and California. *Corylus cornuta* is named from its fruit, which is a nut enclosed in a husk with a tubular extension 2-4 cm (0.79-1.6 in) long that resembles a beak. Tiny filaments protrude from the husk and may stick into, and irritate, skin that contacts them. The spherical nuts, which are surrounded by a hard shell, are edible. There are two varieties: *Corylus cornuta* var. *cornuta* - Eastern Beaked Hazel; small shrub, 4 to 6 m tall; 'beak' longer, 3 cm or more. *Corylus cornuta* var. *californica* - Western Beaked Hazel or California Hazelnut; large shrub, 4 to 15 m tall; 'beak' shorter, usually less than 3 cm."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "beaked hazel plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "WIKIPEDIA:Corylus_cornuta")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13452 <http://eol.org/pages/1147594>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13452 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=19507>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13452 langual:B4506)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "PLANTS:COCO6")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "PLANTS:COCOC")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "PLANTS:COCOC2")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "beaked hazelnut"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "corylus cornuta"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "western hazel"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_13452 "Corylus cornuta Marsh.")
SubClassOf(obo:NCBITaxon_13452 obo:FOODON_03411533)

# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_134520 (Lonicera caerulea)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_134520 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_134520 "*Lonicera caerulea*, the honeyberry, haskap berry, blue-berried honeysuckle, or sweetberry honeysuckle, is a honeysuckle native throughout the cool temperate Northern Hemisphere. The fruit is an edible, blue berry, somewhat rectangular in shape weighing 1.3 to 2.2 grams, and about 1 cm in diameter. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lonicera_caerulea]"@en)
