AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_153348 "*Lepidium meyenii* (maca) is an herbaceous biennial plant of the crucifer family native to the high Andes of Peru. It is grown for its fleshy hypocotyl (a fused hypocotyl and taproot), which is used as a root vegetable and a medicinal herb. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lepidium_meyenii]"@en)
