# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_159421 (Passiflora foetida)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_159421 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_159421 "*Passiflora foetida* (common names: wild maracuja, bush passion fruit, marya-marya, wild water lemon, stinking passionflower, love-in-a-mist or running pop) is a species of passion flower that is native to the southwestern United States, Mexico, the Caribbean, Central America, and much of South America. It has been introduced to tropical regions around the world, such as Southeast Asia and Hawaii. It is a creeping vine like other members of the genus, and yields an edible fruit. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passiflora_foetida]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_159421 "fetid passionflower"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_159421 <http://eol.org/pages/584516>)
