# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_16752 (Houttuynia cordata)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_16752 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_16752 "*Houttuynia cordata*, known as fish mint, fish leaf, lizard tail, chameleon plant, heartleaf, fishwort, and bishop's weed, is one of two species in the genus *Houttuynia* (the other being *H. emeiensis*), a flowering plant native to Japan, Korea, southern China, and Southeast Asia, where it grows in moist, shady places. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houttuynia_cordata]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_16752 "chameleon-plant plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_16752 <http://eol.org/pages/595460>)
