# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 (Mobula birostris)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "A species of ray in the family Mobulidae, and the largest type of ray in the world."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "Damion Dooley"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "giant oceanic manta ray"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 wikipedia:Giant_oceanic_manta_ray)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 <http://eol.org/pages/206970>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 obo:NCBITaxon_195310)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 langual:B4131)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 asfis:rmb)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "CEC1993:110")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "atlantic manta"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "giant devil ray"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "Manta birostris")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 "Until 2017, giant mantas were classified in the genus Manta, along with the smaller reef manta (Mobula alfredi). DNA testing revealed that both species are more closely related to rays of the genus Mobula than previously thought. As a result, giant mantas were renamed Mobula birostris to reflect the new classification. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_oceanic_manta_ray]"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:NCBITaxon_1983395 obo:FOODON_03412298)

