# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_199623 (Alpinia officinarum)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_199623 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_199623 "*Alpinia officinarum*, known as lesser galangal, is a plant in the ginger family, cultivated in Southeast Asia. The rhizomes, known as galangal, are valued for their sweet spicy flavor and aromatic scent. These are used throughout Asia in curries and perfumes, and were previously used widely in Europe. They are also used as an herbal remedy. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpinia_officinarum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_199623 "lesser galangal plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_199623 <http://eol.org/pages/1126822>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_199623 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?101035>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_199623 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=506514>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_199623 langual:B2938)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_199623 "MANSFELD:3440")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_199623 "PLANTS:ALOF4")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_199623 "Alpinia officinarum Hance")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_199623 "alpinia officinarum"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:NCBITaxon_199623 obo:FOODON_03412971)

