# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_201697 (Pomoxis annularis)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_201697 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_201697 "The white crappie, *Pomoxis annularis* Rafinesque, 1818, is native throughout the eastern half of Canada and the United States, and has been widely introduced in the west as well. The white crappie is generally deep-bodied and silvery in color, with darker vertical stripes. The dorsal fin of the white crappie has six spines. The maximum recorded length for a white crappie in 53.0 cm (21 in), with a maximum weight of almost 2.35 kg (more than 5.18 lb); it can live as long as thirty years. This species prefers slower-moving water, whether a backwater of a small creek or a large lake. Some sources say the White Crappie will overpopulate in lakes less than 1000 acres (4 km²). White Crappie often school around structure such as submerged trees. ("@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_201697 "white crappie"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_201697 "WIKIPEDIA:White_crappie)")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_201697 <http://eol.org/pages/218001>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_201697 langual:B3368)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_201697 asfis:pxr)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_201697 "CEC1993:596")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasNarrowSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_201697 "Pomoxis annularis")
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_201697 "aspledinotus grunniens"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_201697 "pomoxis annularis"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:NCBITaxon_201697 obo:FOODON_03411409)

