# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_210328 (Maclura tricuspidata)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_210328 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_210328 "*Maclura tricuspidata * is a tree native to East Asia, occasionally grown for its fruit, somewhat similar to that of the related mulberry (*Morus* spp.). It is also known by common names including cudrang, mandarin melon berry, silkworm thorn, zhe or che, and Chinese mulberry (but not to be confused with *Morus australis * also known by that name). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maclura_tricuspidata]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_210328 "zhe berry plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_210328 <http://eol.org/pages/488084>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_210328 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?23062>)
