# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_219897 (Syzygium paniculatum)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_219897 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_219897 "The magenta lilly pilly (*Syzygium paniculatum*, syn. *Eugenia paniculata*), also known by the common name magenta cherry, is a broad dense bushy rainforest tree native to New South Wales. Well known as an edible wild fruit with a pleasantly sour apple-like flavour. It is eaten fresh or cooked into jams. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syzygium_paniculatum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_219897 "brush cherry plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_219897 <http://eol.org/pages/2508667>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_219897 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?311402>)
