# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_260145 (Ugni molinae)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_260145 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_260145 "*Ugni molinae*, commonly known as Chilean guava, or strawberry myrtle, is a shrub native to Chile and adjacent regions of southern Argentina. The fruit is sometimes marketed as \"Ugniberry\", as \"New Zealand cranberry\" in New Zealand, and the name \"Tazziberry\" has been trademarked in Australia, but it is not a native plant to these countries. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugni_molinae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_260145 "chilean guava plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_260145 <http://eol.org/pages/5461137>)
