AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_29719 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_29719 "Spearmint (binomial *Mentha spicata*, synonym *Mentha viridis*), also known as garden mint, common mint, lamb mint and mackerel mint, is a species of mint native to much of Europe and Asia (Middle East, Himalayas, China etc.), and naturalized in parts of northern and western Africa, North America, and South America, as well as various oceanic islands. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spearmint]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_29719 "spearmint plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_29719 <http://eol.org/pages/579697>)
