# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_32219 (Amelanchier alnifolia)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_32219 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_32219 "*Amelanchier alnifolia*, the saskatoon, Pacific serviceberry, western serviceberry, alder-leaf shadbush, dwarf shadbush, chuckley pear, or western juneberry, is a shrub with edible berry-like fruit, native to North America from Alaska across most of western Canada and in the western and north-central United States. Historically, it was also called pigeon berry."@en)
