AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_34814 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_34814 "The mahi-mahi or common dolphinfish (Coryphaena hippurus) is a surface-dwelling ray-finned fish found in off-shore temperate, tropical, and subtropical waters worldwide. Also widely called dorado and dolphin, it is one of two members of the Coryphaenidae family, the other being the pompano dolphinfish."@en)
