# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_3559 (Chenopodium album)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_3559 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_3559 "*Chenopodium album* is a fast-growing weedy annual plant in the genus *Chenopodium*.
Though cultivated in some regions, the plant is elsewhere considered a weed. Common names include lamb's quarters, melde, goosefoot and fat-hen, though the latter two are also applied to other species of the genus Chenopodium, for which reason it is often distinguished as white goosefoot.It is sometimes also called pigweed.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chenopodium_album]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_3559 "lamb's quarter plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_3559 <http://eol.org/pages/587522>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_3559 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?10178>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_3559 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=20592>)
