# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_3673 (Momordica charantia)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_3673 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_3673 "*Momordica charantia*, known as bitter melon, bitter gourd, bitter squash, or balsam-pear, is a tropical and subtropical vine of the family *Cucurbitaceae*, widely grown in Asia, Africa, and the Caribbean for its edible fruit. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momordica_charantia]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_3673 "bitter melon plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_3673 <http://eol.org/pages/584304>)
