# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_39304 (Erignathus barbatus)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_39304 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_39304 "The bearded seal (*Erignathus barbatus*), also called the square flipper seal, is a medium-sized pinniped that is found in and near to the Arctic Ocean. Bearded seals are a primary food source for polar bears and for the Inuit of the Arctic coast. The Inuktitut name for the seal is Ugyuk or Oogrook or Oogruk."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_39304 "bearded seal"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_39304 "WIKIPEDIA:Bearded_seal")
