# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_39352 (Origanum vulgare)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_39352 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_39352 "Oregano (*Origanum vulgare*) is a flowering plant in the mint family (*Lamiaceae*). It is native to temperate Western and Southwestern Eurasia and the Mediterranean region. It is sometimes called wild marjoram, and its close relative, *O. majorana*, is known as sweet marjoram. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oregano]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_39352 "oregano plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_39352 <http://eol.org/pages/579367>)
