# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_39388 (Verbascum thapsus)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_39388 "*Verbascum*, common name mullein (also known as velvet plant), is a genus of about 250 species of flowering plants in the figwort family *Scrophulariaceae*. They are native to Europe and Asia, with the highest species diversity in the Mediterranean. Mullein or \"mullein leaf\" often refers to the leaves of *Verbascum thapsus*, the great or common mullein, which is frequently used in herbal medicine.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verbascum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:NCBITaxon_39388 <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-8844-9165>)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_39388 "mullein plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:date obo:NCBITaxon_39388 "2021-08-19T00:01:41Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_39388 <http://eol.org/pages/60976>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_39388 langual:B5146)
