AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_395311 "*Rumex arcticus*, commonly known as Arctic Dock or Sourdock, is a perennial flowering plant that is native to Alaska. Its leaves are an important part of the diet of native Alaskans such as the Yupik people, who include it in various dishes such as akutaq."@en)
