# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_4505 (Coix lacryma-jobi)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_4505 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_4505 "Job's Tears, Coixseed, adlay, or adlai, is a tall grain-bearing tropical plant of the family *Poaceae* (grass family) native to East Asia and peninsular Malaysia but elsewhere cultivated in gardens as an annual. The variety *Coix lacryma-jobi* var. *ma-yuen* is harvested as a cereal crop and is used medicinally in parts of Asia. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Job%27s_tears]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_4505 "job's tears plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_4505 <http://eol.org/pages/1114853>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_4505 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?11129>)
