# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_58041 (Pinus cembra)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_58041 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_58041 "*Pinus cembra*, also known as Swiss pine, Swiss stone pine or Arolla pine or Austrian stone pine or just Stone pine, is a species of pine tree that grows in the Alps and Carpathian Mountains of central Europe. The seeds are also harvested and sold as pine nuts. Pine cones cut into slices are used to flavor Schnapps. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinus_cembra]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_58041 "swiss pine plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_58041 <http://eol.org/pages/1033596>)
