# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_641111 (Pleuronectes quadrituberculatus)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_641111 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_641111 "Alaska plaice (*Pleuronectes quadrituberculatus*) is a saltwater fish that live in the North Pacific Ocean. Like most flatfish, they live on the bottom of the continental shelf, up to 600 metres deep. Their geographic range is from the Gulf of Alaska in the east, to the Chukchi Sea in the north, to the Sea of Japan in the west."@en)
