# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_654836 (Momordica dioica)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_654836 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_654836 "*Momordica dioica*, Bristly Balsam Pear, commonly known as spiny gourd or spine gourd and also known as prickly carolaho, Teasle gourd, kantola, is a species of flowering plant in the gourd family. It is used as a vegetable in all regions of India and some parts in South Asia. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momordica_dioica]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_654836 "spine gourd plant"@en)
