# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_6715 (Astacus astacus)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_6715 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_6715 "*Astacus astacus*, the European crayfish, noble crayfish or broad-fingered crayfish, is the most common species of crayfish in Europe. Like other crayfish, The European crayfish is restricted to freshwater, living only in unpolluted streams, rivers and lakes. It is found from France throughout central Europe, to the Balkan peninsula, and north as far as parts of the British Isles, Scandinavia, and the western parts of the former Soviet Union. 
*Astacus astacus* is susceptible to the crayfish plague carried by the invasive American species *Pacifastacus leniusculus*, and is therefore listed as \"vulnerable\" by the IUCN Red List of Threatened Species. Citation: Sket, B. 1996. Astacus astacus. 
In: IUCN 2006. 2006 IUCN Red List of Threatened Species. <www.iucnredlist.org>. Downloaded on 26 January 2007."@en)
