# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_72648 (Tacca leontopetaloides)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_72648 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_72648 "*Tacca leontopetaloides* is a species of flowering plant in the yam family *Dioscoreaceae*, that is native to tropical Africa, South Asia, Southeast Asia, northern Australia, New Guinea, Samoa, Micronesia, and Fiji. The tubers of Polynesian arrowroot contain starch, making it an important food source for many Pacific Island cultures, primarily for the inhabitants of low islands and atolls. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tacca_leontopetaloides]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_72648 "polynesian arrowrrot plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_72648 <http://eol.org/pages/345447>)
AnnotationAssertion(go:hasDbXref obo:NCBITaxon_72648 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?70775>)
