# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_74478 (Himanthalia elongata)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_74478 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_74478 "*Himanthalia elongata* is a brown alga in the order *Fucales*, also known by the common names thongweed, sea thong and sea spaghetti. It is found in the north east Atlantic Ocean and the North Sea. 
According to the World Register of Marine Species, *Himanthalia elongata* is the only member of its genus, *Himanthalia* Lyngbye, 1819 [2] and the only member of its family, *Himanthaliaceae* (Kjellman) De Toni, 1891."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_74478 "sea thong"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_74478 "WIKIPEDIA:Himanthalia_elongata")
