# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_75939 (Dallia pectoralis)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_75939 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_75939 "Alaska blackfish are found in swamps, ponds, lakes, and streams with vegetation for cover, in tundra and forested locations not far inland. Their range includes Alaska and the Bering Sea islands. Alaska Natives once ate these fish and fed them to their dogs, catching them in the fall and freezing them for use over winter."@en)
