# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_93934 (Coturnix japonica)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_93934 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_93934 "A species of Old World quail found in East Asia. First considered a subspecies of the common quail, it was distinguished as its own species in 1983. As the Japanese quail is easily managed, fast growing, small in size, and can produce eggs at a high rate, it has been farmed in large quantities across the globe."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_93934 "japanese quail"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_93934 wikipedia:Japanese_quail)
