AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_93977 "*Osmanthus fragrans*, variously known as sweet osmanthus, sweet olive, tea olive, and fragrant olive, is a species native to Asia. In Chinese cuisine, its flowers may be infused with green or black tea leaves to create a scented tea. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osmanthus_fragrans]"@en)
