# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_9838 (Camelus dromedarius)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_9838 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_9838 "The dromedary camel or Arabian camel (*Camelus dromedarius*) is a large, even-toed ungulate with one hump on its back. It was first described by Carl Linnaeus in 1758. The dromedary camel is the second largest member of the camel family after the larger Bactrian camel."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_9838 "dromedary camel"@en)
