AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03303835 "Defined by Codex Alimentarius standard CODEX STAN 280-1973, Anhydrous milkfat is a milk product containing almost no water and non‑fat solids.  Anhydrous milk fat must contain at least 99.8 % milk fat and be made from fresh cream or butter. No additives are allowed, e.g. for neutralization of free fatty acids."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03303835 "https://dairyprocessinghandbook.com/chapter/anhydrous-milk-fat-amf-and-butteroil"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03305145 "A farm-produced crop, usually fruit or vegetable, that is fresh and in the same state as where and when it was harvested."@en)
