AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_371859 "Opuntia ficus-indica (prickly pear) is a species of cactus that has long been a domesticated crop plant grown in agricultural economies throughout arid and semiarid parts of the world. Likely having originated in Mexico, O. ficus-indica is the most widespread and most commercially important cactus."@en)
