AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_8853 "The Canada goose (*Branta canadensis*) is a large wild goose species with a black head and neck, white patches on the face, and a brown body. Native to arctic and temperate regions of North America, its migration occasionally reaches northern Europe."@en)
